---
args: {"productions": "AccessibleProduction[]", "edit": "AccessibilityEdit", "mediaState": "AccessibleMediaState | null"}
returns: "AccessibleMediaReview"
---
1. Bind prior to mediaState or AccessibleMediaState { revision: 0, scenes: [], revealBoundaries: [], windows: [], cues: [], editHistory: [], validatedReceiptIds: [], releasedArtifactIds: [] }. Bind scenes = reconstructSceneInformation(productions, edit.sceneEvidence). Bind reveals = preserveAudienceKnowledge(scenes, edit.sceneEvidence). Separate observable information from its later narrative significance.
2. Bind dependencies = identifyStableSceneEdits(edit.sourceDelta, scenes, prior). Bind retimedCues = retimeAffectedCues(dependencies, prior.cues). Preserve unaffected scene/cue identities; an edit before scene S9 shifts its dependent cues without inventing new scene identity.
3. Bind windows = identifyChannelWindows(scenes, edit.sceneEvidence, edit.styleAndConsent). Bind allocation = assignEssentialInformation(scenes, reveals, windows, edit.styleAndConsent). A scene with no description gap requires an approved alternative channel or edit request, not overlap with essential dialogue.
4. Bind candidateCues initially to unaffected prior cues and retimedCues whose information and reveal order remain unchanged. For each remaining channel assignment with an actual window call writeObservableCue(scene, channelWindow, reveals, edit.styleAndConsent), adding its actual returned cue. An assignment without a window becomes an edit request rather than an invented timed cue. Verify off-screen speaker identity from actual source evidence and describe visible actions without invented motives or future meaning.
5. Bind findings = challengeSynchronizedExperience(scenes, allocation, candidateCues, reveals, edit.playerReceipts or an empty collection). Check essential information across transitions as well as individual cues. Keep exact time/overlap checks and independent narrative/usability review distinct.
6. Bind matchedReceipts to supplied target-format/player receipts whose source edition, actual artifact and cue inventory match these candidateCues and whose required checks pass. Bind nextMedia as AccessibleMediaState { revision: advance only for actual scene/edit/cue/receipt changes, scenes, revealBoundaries: reveals, windows, cues: candidateCues, editHistory: prior.editHistory plus dependencies once by changed source identity, validatedReceiptIds: prior valid IDs plus actual matched receipt IDs, releasedArtifactIds: prior historical IDs plus only actual delivered artifact IDs from matching receipts }. Return AccessibleMediaReview { mediaState: nextMedia, proposedCues: new and retimed candidateCues, editRequests: unsupported allocation windows plus findings requiring a source edit, missingEssentialFacts: exact fact identities unresolved in allocation or findings, staleCueIds: exact cue identities invalidated by dependencies, deliveryArtifactIds: actually matched delivered artifact IDs, releaseBlocked: true when findings, missing essential facts, unsafe timing or required receipt validation remain unresolved }. Plausible timing alone does not establish delivery.
